Some more random messages from recent games...

The tin of warhorse meat misses the saddled warhorse.
What do you want to throw? [$ar or ?*]
In what direction?
The saddled warhorse devours an orange.
The saddled warhorse picks up a tin of warhorse meat.


And here it seems the RNG is not so evil as usually presumed...

You fall into a pit!  You land on a set of sharp iron spikes!
There is a spiked pit here.  You see here a spellbook of levitation.
K - a spellbook of levitation.

...he provided at least some means to escape.


I'd certainly drone as well if they'd put me in a tin alive...

It is not so easy to open this tin.  You hear an angry drone.
You succeed in opening the tin.  It smells like titanotheres.


Is this the last act of Samual Beckett's "Waiting for Godot"...?

You stop waiting.  You feel wise!  You must have been very observant.


Gaining level is not quite compatible with calling for help...

The invisible Baalzebub drinks a potion of gain level!
In a cloud of smoke, a djinni emerges!  The djinni speaks.
"It is about time."  The djinni vanishes.

...but the djinn refused - he realized who would win the fight.


I hate it when major demons are created, and created with amulets...

You kill the invisible Dispater!
But wait...  The invisible Dispater's medallion begins to glow!
The invisible Dispater looks much better!


